' ─────────────────── Composition / Association (solid line) ───────────────────
Feedback "1" *-- "0..*" FeedbackParticipantRating : contains >
Patient "1" -- "0..*" Feedback : submits >
Appointment "1" -- "0..1" Feedback : is rated by >
CareSession "1" -- "0..1" Feedback : is rated by >
Doctor "1" -- "0..*" Feedback : is rated in >
User "1" -- "0..*" Feedback : rated as nurse in >
FeedbackRequest +-- ParticipantRating

' ── Hidden edges: stack the repository interfaces vertically instead of
'    letting Graphviz spread them across one very wide row ──────────────────
FeedbackRepository -[hidden]down- AppointmentRepository
AppointmentRepository -[hidden]down- CareSessionRepository
CareSessionRepository -[hidden]down- MedicalRecordRepository
MedicalRecordRepository -[hidden]down- LabOrderRepository
LabOrderRepository -[hidden]down- UserRepository
UserRepository -[hidden]down- PatientRepository

' ─────────────────── Note ───────────────────
note top of Feedback
  {xor} — exactly one of appointment / careSession must be set.
  Enforced twice: submitFeedback() rejects a request carrying
  both or neither id, and the database repeats the rule as
  CK_feedbacks_subject (appointment_id + care_session_id = 1).
end note

note right of FeedbackServiceImpl
  Validation order inside submitAppointmentFeedback():
  1. ownership — appointment.patient.id == patientId
  2. UC-46 PRE-2 — appointment.status == COMPLETED
  3. BR-21 — existsByAppointment_Id(...) == false
  submitCareSessionFeedback() applies the same three
  checks against CareSession.status == "COMPLETED".
end note

note bottom of FeedbackParticipantRating
  Composition (filled diamond): @OneToMany with
  cascade = ALL + orphanRemoval = true — a per-person
  score cannot exist outside its Feedback.
  Rows with a null rating are skipped, so the list may
  be empty (0..*) even when the form offered participants.
end note

note bottom of Feedback
  status is a String, always created as "PENDING" (POST-1).
  The database allows {PENDING, APPROVED, HIDDEN}
  (CK_feedbacks_status), but the code never writes the other
  two — no approve/hide transition is implemented yet.
  rating is checked twice: @Valid 1..5 on the request
  (UC-46 E1) and CK_feedbacks_rating in the database.
end note

note right of FeedbackController
  patientId is resolved from the JWT principal via
  resolvePatientId(), never from a request parameter,
  so a patient cannot rate or read someone else's visit.
end note

' A legend does not take part in the graph layout, so the long
' deviation list no longer stretches the diagram sideways.
legend bottom
  **Deviations from the SRS — need a decision**
  1. BR-21 (one feedback per appointment) is enforced ONLY in the service layer via
     existsByAppointment_Id / existsByCareSession_Id. ecms_schema.sql declares no UNIQUE
     index on appointment_id or care_session_id, so two concurrent submissions can still
     race past the check — unlike the {xor} and rating rules, which the database guards.
  2. Normal Flow step 1 says the system automatically sends a feedback request "via Portal
     and email" once the visit is COMPLETED — no such trigger or email exists in the code;
     the Patient must open the form themselves.
  3. The SRS covers appointments only; the code also accepts feedback on a CareSession
     (rating the Nurse instead of the Doctor). The SRS should be extended to match.
  4. getVisitParticipants() returns Map<String,Object> rather than a DTO, so there is no
     explicit data contract for the frontend.
endlegend

@enduml
